WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:06.606
-[ Whistling ]

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.910
Oh, hey, Liam.
Good to see you.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.246
-Hey, good to see you, too.
How you doing?

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.580
-I've been doing great,
doing well.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.683
How about you?
-Yeah, doing well, too.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.818
-That's great, that's cool, man.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.854
Wow.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.524
I got to tell you, you're great
in the "Avengers" movies.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:29.162
I just can't wait.
And I'm freaking out.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:32.732
-Oh.
-Great, man.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:36.969
-Yeah, sorry. That's actually
my brother Chris.

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:39.238
-Oh.
Oh, my God.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:40.640
Are you kidding me?
How embarrassing.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.675
I'm so sorry.
-No, that's all right.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.812
-You, though,
were great in "Westworld."

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:51.184
-Yeah, that was -- that was
actually my other brother, Luke.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.719
Yeah,
I'm the other, other brother.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:54.954
-Oh.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:54.954 --> 00:01:02.862
-[ Chuckles nervously ]
-That's funny.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.998
You know, my wife
is a huge fan of your show.

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:09.736
You should see our DVR --
nothing but "Big Bang Theory."

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.838
Bazinga!
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.943
-That's not me.
That's, uh --

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.811
That's Jim Parsons.
But I get that a lot.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.980
I get that a lot.
So it's kind of...

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.716
-Right, yeah, Jim Parsons.
-Mm.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.019
-Yeah, sorry about that.
-Don't worry about it.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.653
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.957
I got to be honest, though,
I don't know how you do it.

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.792
I mean, balancing your career,
your two kids.

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:37.597
Telling that multi-part story
about how you met their mother.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.832
Must be tough.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:44.770
-That's Ted Mosby
you're thinking of.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.406
"How I Met Your Mother."

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.973
I'm sure you get asked this
all the time.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.174
But do you ever
get off the island

00:01:49.174 --> 00:01:51.911
and deliver that FedEx package?

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.246
The volleyball and...
-Ah, yeah.

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:56.049
That's Tom Hanks
from "Castaway."

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:59.519
-Mnh-mnh.
Mnh-mnh.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:02.455
-Speaking of Tom Hanks, though,
my favorite rom-com of all time,

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.391
you know, obviously,
is you and Tom Hanks,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.693
where you're bookstore rivals

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.361
and you fall in love
through e-mail?

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:10.696
That's great.
-Oh.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:12.465
-What's the name
of that one again?

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.767
What's the name of that movie,
you and Tom Hanks?

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.635
-"You've Got Mail."
-Yes.

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:18.470
"You've Got Mail."
-No, that's a good movie.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.440
-It really is.
-That's actually Meg Ryan.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.710
-Really, though, is it?
-Um...I think so.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.214
-Huh.
[ Elevator bell dings ]

00:02:29.214 --> 00:02:31.951
-What floor you going to?
-Seven.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:36.088
-Me too, me too.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:37.289
Patriots quarterback?

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:38.624
-"Bachelor" contestant,
season 10?

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:40.726
-"Marvelous Mrs. Maisel"?
-Founder of Facebook?

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.027
-Member of BTS?

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:44.897
-Large green giant,
leafy toga, sells frozen peas?

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:47.032
-Large green ogre,
friends with a donkey?

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:48.400
-Semi-aquatic egg-laying mammal

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.771
native to
Eastern Australia/Tasmania?

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:52.772
-Dad?

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.373
[ Elevator bell dings ]

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.407
[ Cellphone rings ]

00:02:55.407 --> 00:02:56.876
-Ooh, should probably
take this, mate.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.010
It's good seeing you, though.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.878
-Hey, good to see you, too,
buddy. Bye.

00:02:59.878 --> 00:03:02.882
-Babe, just met your favorite
person, Jimmy Kimmel.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:06.052
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.387
[ Cheers and applause ]

